 **Parameters:**
 - **isolevel:** The scalar threshold defining the surface. Vertices with values $<$ isolevel are considered "inside" (or "outside" depending on convention, must match lookup table) [S2, unofficial].
-- **adaptive:** If true, uses linear interpolation based on field values; if false, uses midpoint (0.5) for all intersections [S2, unofficial].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Topological Ambiguity:** The standard algorithm has 15 distinct special cases for surface intersections, and certain configurations (e.g., saddle points) can lead to topological errors (tunnels or holes) if the lookup table assumes a simple topology [S1, S4, unofficial].
-- **Precision:** Division by zero occurs if both vertices of an edge have identical scalar values. A guard check is required [S2, unofficial].
+- **Topological Ambiguity:** The standard algorithm has 15 distinct special cases for surface intersections [S2, unofficial].
 - **Vertex Sharing:** The basic algorithm does not share vertices between triangles; each triangle outputs 3 new vertices, leading to higher memory usage and potential normal discontinuities at shared edges [S2, unofficial].
 
